# ---- Secrets / dev-only files: NEVER commit ----
token.txt
.env
config.json
config.json.*
mirror_session.json
mirror_session.json.*
serve.txt
serve.log

# ---- Private dev notes: reverse-engineering ledger, internal maps. NEVER publish ----
private/

# ---- Gallery server generated files ----
pixai_backup/gallery/

# ---- Any --out directory's generated files, by name, not just the default `pixai_backup/`.
# `pixai_backup/` below only matches THAT literal name; a custom `--out my_dir` doesn't
# match it, so its catalog.db/images/gallery/etc. would otherwise show up in git status.
# These are unanchored (no leading slash) so they catch the same well-known out_dir-
# relative structure at any depth, regardless of the out_dir's name -- same trick
# jobs.jsonl already used below (before this, jobs.jsonl was the ONLY thing generalized
# this way; catalog.db and the rest still leaked under a custom --out).
catalog.db
catalog.csv
gallery/
images/
videos/
imported/
_duplicates/
organize_manifest.csv
audit_report.csv
verify_report.csv
raw_tasks.jsonl

# ---- Job activity log (append-only registry the Jobs card reads; runtime state) ----
# pixai_backup/ is already ignored below; these catch any out_dir that lands in the repo.
jobs.jsonl
jobs.jsonl.tmp

# ---- Personal output: your images, prompts, catalogs ----
# Contains your generated images, prompt text, and dates. Keep out of git.
pixai_backup/
*.webp
# Uncomment if you ever keep loose exports in the repo root and want them ignored:
# *.png
# *.jpg
# *.jpeg

# ---- Python ----
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# ---- Working dashboard artifact (Claude+owner reference; not project documentation) ----
docs/DASHBOARD.html

# ---- Loom Node toolchain (loom/package.json) ----
loom/node_modules/

# ---- Editor / OS ----
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- Stray artifact: a root file literally named HEAD, content just "OUTPUT".
# Real cause (found 2026-07-22): tests/test_panel.py's ffmpeg-mocking FakeProc
# patches subprocess.Popen globally with no command guard, and create_app()
# shells `git rev-parse --short HEAD` through that same patched Popen -- for
# THAT call argv[-1] is the literal string "HEAD". Fixed at the source (the
# FakeProc now only writes when argv[0] == "ffmpeg"); this stays as a backstop
# in case it ever regenerates some other way. Anchored to root so it never
# shadows .git/HEAD or subdir HEADs. ----
/HEAD

# ---- Claude Code: local browser-preview launch config (machine-local dev-server
# definition, points at a local port). Scoped to the file, not all of .claude/, so
# genuinely shareable project config (agents, hooks) can still be tracked later. ----
/.claude/launch.json

# Agent worktrees. Claude Code checks out throwaway copies of the repo under here, each a full
# tree, so an untracked-file listing fills with thousands of duplicates of the project. Scoped to
# this ONE directory for the same reason launch.json above is: .claude/setup.sh is tracked and must
# stay that way.
#
# Not cosmetic. On 2026-07-26 a rename script used rglob(), which does not consult gitignore, and
# rewrote files INSIDE five live agent worktrees while a workflow was reading them -- corrupting
# all five mid-run. Ignoring the directory does not by itself stop a script that walks the
# filesystem directly, but it does stop these trees showing up as repo content, and it documents
# that nothing in here is ever project state.
/.claude/worktrees/

# Ephemeral design mockups: throwaway single-file HTML built to verify a design
# before implementing it (the locked pixel source lives in the Claude artifact, not
# here). Never committed -- they would rot instantly against the real surface.
static/_mockup_*.html

# Branding art and the selections that go with it. Moved out of the library folder to the app
# root on 2026-07-26, which puts USER CONTENT inside a git-managed directory for the first time --
# so this entry ships in the SAME commit as the move. Without it the first person to drop a mascot
# into a slot sees their own art as untracked repo content, and `git add -A` is already banned here
# for exactly that class of accident.
#
# The folders are empty by design on a fresh install: finding them is the "Under the Hood" easter
# egg, so they must exist and must not carry anyone else's art.
/branding/
/branding.json
/branding_slots.json

# The asset container (tools/build_container.py -> moonglade.dat). NOT committed BY DECISION
# (docs/DECISIONS.md "The asset container, re-scoped from scratch", 2026-08-10): delivery is a
# GitHub Release asset fetched on first run -- Releases have no bandwidth caps, git/LFS does.
# This entry implements that decision; it is not a privacy call.
/moonglade.dat
# Materialized-from-container cache for things needing a REAL file on disk (the Desktop-shortcut
# writer's .ico -- PowerShell reads IconLocation off disk). Regenerable, like branding/_thumbs/.
/_container_cache/

# The Claude Design handoff package (design_handoff_moonglade_suite): DC prototype
# surfaces, drift report, and ASSETS INCLUDING THE OWNER'S BRANDING ART -- which is
# deliberately machine-local (see /branding/ above) and must never reach this public
# repo. Kept beside the code as the implementation reference for the gallery-era
# redesign; master copies are the zips the owner downloaded from Claude Design.
/design_handoff/

# The REPO-ROOT gallery/ is the React frontend's SOURCE (the /next pilot) -- not an
# out-dir's runtime gallery folder, which is what the unanchored `gallery/` above
# guards at any depth. Re-include the source tree; keep its node_modules out. dist/
# is committed on purpose, same as loom/dist -- the other machine and the run-copy
# work without npm.
!/gallery/
/gallery/node_modules/

# Local triage worksheet from the 2026-07-27 adversarial code review. Working material:
# findings get parsed out into Decisions.md and the file is deleted. Never committed --
# it is a snapshot of defects, and a stale copy in the repo would be exactly the kind of
# contradictory state doc this review was scoped to avoid.
/bugreview.md
